// Jahshaka's DDGI diffuse INTENSITY — the one thing upstream's IrradianceField
// has no knob for (GI_UNIFIED_SPEC.md §4 P1 / addendum item 2 — that is the
// earlier spec of the program now called PHOTON; SPECS/PHOTON_SPEC.md is live).
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Binding an IrradianceField makes HlmsPbs set
// `VctDisableDiffuse` (OgreHlmsPbs.cpp:1846-1850): DDGI does not ADD to voxel
// cone tracing's diffuse, it REPLACES it — and the P0 spike measured the
// replacement at ~13x dimmer than the (over-bright, leak-prone) VCT diffuse it
// takes over from. Every scene therefore gets markedly darker the moment the
// field binds, and `IrradianceFieldSettings` carries nothing to scale it with.
// So the scalar is OURS, applied at the last line of upstream's own piece, and
// it rides the pass buffer (a const-buffer write, never a shader rebuild) so
// the author can turn the dial without a recompile.
// THE CAGE IS ONE TEXT (PHOTON-7 stage 7, 7-2): the clamp, the sample point's bias, the window's slot, the front share
// and the confidence that were this file's five hooks into the pixel's cage are jah_field_read.glsl's (the piece
// JahFieldRead), the cage the PBS piece (PhotonIfd_piece_ps.any, an owned copy of upstream's) and the screen-probe
// gather's integrate both read. What this file keeps is the HOST'S part: the fallback where the field's confidence
// fades. (The gate that declined the cage under a gathered pixel is gone with the pass that held both: a pass that reads
// the gather binds no field, PHOTON-7 7-5 - the integrate composes it.)
//
// CAUTION, the same one JahFog and JahVct carry, and this file cost the lane a
// full test run by ignoring it: the Hlms parser does NOT respect // comments —
// an at-directive written inside a comment is EXECUTED, and a stray parenthesis
// after one is a syntax error that silently drops every definition in the file
// (the shader still compiles; it just uses upstream's piece, so the symptom is
// "my override does nothing"). Every directive is therefore named in WORDS
// above, never written with its at-sign.
//
// THE SKY IS IN THE FIELD (PHOTON-ENV-1). The field's generation job gives
// every probe ray that escapes the voxels the ONE ENVIRONMENT in its direction at
// its own aperture (jahEnvCone, jah_environment.glsl), weighted by the ray's
// escape fraction `1 - min( 1, opacity / 0.95 )`, and the cosine integration
// carries it into the irradiance atlas beside the bounce: a probe's irradiance
// IS the sky it sees plus the light the voxels hold, one integral, and this file
// reads nothing else. The read-time `SH x sky visibility` term that stood here
// (and its dial, and the escape channel of the depth atlas it read) is gone: a
// sealed room's interior rays all stop in its walls, so its probes hold no sky.
//
// jahIfd.yz carry the field's Y and Z probe counts, which upstream's own render
// params do NOT contain (only Nx and Nx*Ny reach the shader,
// OgreIrradianceField.cpp:812-813); the cage clamp below needs all three.
//
// THE THIRD THING THAT IS NOT UPSTREAM'S: THE FIELD'S EDGE
// (ENGINE_CACHE_POLICY_SPEC.md P9, re-scoped 2026-09-13; the owner's report was
// "the Grand Showroom 2's roof shows texture maps", and the diagnosis is
// spikes/showroom2-roof/ + spikes/e3-ifdedge/).
//
// THE DEFECT IS UPSTREAM'S AND IT IS TWO DEFECTS. (1) The cage loop's comment
// says "clamp to the probe grid boundary" and no clamp is performed, here or in
// the world->grid map (OgreIrradianceField.cpp:794-812), so a pixel outside the
// grid indexes past it and getProbeIdx's FLAT index wraps into another probe
// row -- a surface above a building is handed the irradiance of a probe inside
// it. (2) Even with the cage clamped the field answers everywhere, because the
// sum is NORMALISED by sumIfdWeight: a pixel a hundred metres outside the
// volume still gets the border probes' irradiance at full strength, since
// crushing all eight weights only renormalises the same eight probes. The
// Chebyshev visibility test cannot rescue either case, and that was MEASURED
// rather than assumed (the note in the loop).
//
// WHAT IS DONE ABOUT IT, in three parts, none of which costs a sample (the first two in jah_field_read.glsl):
//   * the CLAMP the comment promises;
//   * a CONFIDENCE in [0, 1] that is 1 wherever the field has something to say
//     and 0 where it does not -- zero outside the read region (the window less
//     its guard band), and zero on a surface with no probe on its own side;
//   * a FALLBACK (this file), so that "the field says nothing" means "what this pixel had
//     before a field was ever bound" rather than "black": the voxel-cone
//     ambient term that binding a field deletes.
// Inside the field the confidence is exactly 1 and every frame is what it was:
// gi.modes, gi.ddgi, gi.ddgi_ambient and gi.ddgi_raster print identical numbers
// with this file and without it.
//
// SCOPE: the whole file is gated on the `irradiance_field` property, which
// HlmsPbs sets only while a field is bound. With no field bound (every scene
// that has not opted in, which in P1 is all of them by default) not one line of
// this file reaches the generated shader, and undefining a piece that was never
// defined is a no-op.

@property( irradiance_field )

// ---- THE TERMS THAT COMPLEMENT THE FIELD -------------------------------
//
// Inserted AFTER upstream's composite add, in this order, so the accumulation
// order of every term in this file is what it was when the body was a copy.
@piece( custom_ps_ifdCagePost )
@property( vct_num_probes )
	// AND THE FALLBACK: WHERE THE FIELD'S CONFIDENCE FADES, THE VOXEL CHAIN'S OWN BOUNCE (PHOTON_SPEC 13 G3, option
	// (a) as decided; PHOTON-7 10-3 R3: one rule for any cascade count). The field rides cascade 0, and the voxels
	// around it hold real, voxelised, light-injected radiance out to the outermost box; the two terms are blended by
	// the field's confidence - the field inside its window, the cones outside it, never both: envColourD receives
	// exactly ONE diffuse-GI term in every regime. (A SINGLE VOLUME took the environment's diffuse there instead -
	// "what an unoccluded surface had before the field" - which is the sky through a wall wherever the field's window
	// ends inside a building; that arm and the gate it rode, vct_disable_diffuse, are deleted: the cone block is never
	// disabled by a field, PhotonPassBinding no longer sets the property.)
	float ifdFallbackAmbient = 1.0 - ifdConfidence;
	//
	// `vctDiffuse` is the cone block's result, and it already carries the sky:
	// every cone's escape reads the one environment in its own direction
	// (Vct_piece_ps.any), as every probe ray of the field does, so the ring gets
	// precisely the picture it had before any field existed, weighted out as the
	// pixel enters the field's reach.
	//
	// THE CONES ARE MARCHED ONLY WHERE THAT WEIGHT IS ABOVE ZERO (SPEED-GPU, audit PH-2).
	// Inside the field the confidence is exactly 1, the weight exactly 0, and four whole
	// cone marches per pixel used to be multiplied by it - most of the screen. The weight
	// is known before the march now, so the march runs where it is read and nowhere else:
	// the same arithmetic in the same order where it runs, and an add of nothing where it
	// does not.
	if( ifdFallbackAmbient > 0.0 )
	{
		float3 jahConeBiasLS;
		float4 jahConeOriginLS;
		const float3 jahConePosLS = jahVctPixelStart( inPs.pos, jahConeBasis, passBuf.vctProbeParams,
													  jahConeBiasLS, jahConeOriginLS );
		jahVctDiffuse( vctDiffuse, jahConePosLS, jahConeOriginLS, jahConeBasis,
					   passBuf.vctProbeParams );
		pixelData.envColourD.xyz += vctDiffuse.xyz * ifdFallbackAmbient;
	}
@end

@end

@end
